## Why This Is Asked
Advanced offline-first crash reporting with privacy controls and cross-process boundaries is common at scale. It tests IPC design, data governance, and testing discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Android isolated processes and AIDL APIs
- Privacy-preserving data handling (PII redaction, hashing)
- Local buffering with encrypted storage
- Background upload with WorkManager, TLS + pinning
- Per-user opt-in and auditability

## Code Example
```java
// Example AIDL surface (pseudo)
interface ICrashReporter {
  void reportCrash(in CrashDump dump);
  void flush();
  void setUserOptIn(boolean optIn);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for IPC boundary violations and data leakage?
- How would you quantify privacy risk under diverse crash formats?

